  "instance_name": "glorification_of_violence",
  "label": "Glorification of Violence",
  "description": "This refers to the act of portraying violence in a positive, heroic, or admirable light, often to justify or normalize it. The meme uses the imagery of demonic figures standing triumphantly on a cliff, which is a common trope in media to depict villains or perpetrators of evil acts. The juxtaposition with the text 'me and the boys after killing innocent people' implies a glorification of the act, which requires understanding of how media and culture can portray violence in a way that may be perceived as heroic or triumphant.",
